From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ARongvv <arongvv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] audio: fix ES8311 single-byte register read length

The ES8311 register read helper stores data in a single uint8_t but requested
12 bytes from I2C.  Limit the transfer to the destination object size to
avoid a stack buffer overflow during codec initialization and configuration.

---
 drivers/audio/es8311.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/audio/es8311.c b/drivers/audio/es8311.c
index 33b89476b9b..dc099da7647 100644
--- a/drivers/audio/es8311.c
+++ b/drivers/audio/es8311.c
@@ -248,7 +248,7 @@ uint8_t es8311_readreg(FAR struct es8311_dev_s *priv, uint8_t regaddr)
       msg[1].addr      = priv->lower->address;
       msg[1].flags     = I2C_M_READ;
       msg[1].buffer    = &data;
-      msg[1].length    = 12;
+      msg[1].length    = sizeof(data);
 
       /* Read the register data. The returned value is the number messages
        * completed.
-- 
2.47.0

